# The order of inserts when the metadata queue is in play, as in a daemon: a first pass as localhost's (every alert
# linked, unlinked and linked again, all queued) whose own saves go at once; the store job then inserts the queued
# entries after them, so the rows of health_log_detail are not in the order of their unique ids, and each queued
# insert points its alarm's last_transition_id back at an older entry until the alarm's next insert. With the
# host's ACLK sync configuration in place each insert also writes the alarm's row of alert_queue.
database real
rules tests/corpus/sql/save.conf
queue 1
aclk-config 1
chart loop.s loop.s_name loop.sql disks things 1
label loop.s kind ssd
var loop.s v 10
pending host-recheck
pending chart-recheck loop.s
clock 0
pass 0
clock 1
pass 1
clock 2
store
var loop.s v 70
clock 3
pass 3
clock 4
pass 4
clock 5
alarm-log 0
